Kill Me Baby!

00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:57.120
kondo ha wasa wasa

00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:57.120
Now then! Rustle! Rustle!

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:58.330
Kill Me Baby!

00:01:58.330 --> 00:01:59.420
nan dayo naamin

00:01:58.330 --> 00:01:59.420
What now, Naamin?

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:00.670
Kill Me Baby!

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:01.880
mada mada camo camo

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:01.880
Still going! Come on! Come on!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.130
Kill Me Baby!

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:04.340
Kill Me Baby!

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:05.510
Kill Me Baby!

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:06.760
Kill Me Baby!

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.430
don!

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.430
Boom!

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:14.620
Break time.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.200
Hey, Sonya-chan, teach me some more cool moves!

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.720
You're still on about that?

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:26.010
My moves aren't really for self-defense, you know.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.420
I know.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:30.470
They're assassination moves, not martial arts.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.380
Do you want to kill someone?

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:36.590
Not really. I just want to be
prepared if anything happens.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:43.140
<i>Truth is, I just want to learn her moves
so I can counter them next time.</i>

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:45.640
Anyway, I hope you can teach me well—

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:46.050
No way.

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:47.300
So fast?!

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.520
Besides, what do I get from teaching you?

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:58.990
By doing this good deed for me,
your sins in this world shall be forgiven.

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:00.820
Who the heck do you think you are?!

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:01.910
Don't show them to me!

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:03.910
I want you to teach them to me!

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:07.290
C'mon. I'll treat you to something later.

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:08.620
No thanks.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:11.100
Then I shall pledge my loyalty to you.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.750
You're not even being serious.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:15.690
Just teach me <i>something</i>!

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:16.670
You're so persistent.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:18.960
I'll stop if you teach me.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.320
If not, I'll just ask you again tomorrow.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:21.080
And again the next day.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.950
From morning till night, I'll ask!

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.620
Wow, you're annoying.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:26.520
No helping it.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:30.070
All right. I'll teach you a special move.

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:31.290
Keep it a secret.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:35.190
You roll across the ground and tackle your opponent.

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:33.570
Strong!

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:35.190
Strong!

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:37.610
This one's called the Super Rolling Crush.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:36.860
Strong!

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:38.400
Strong!

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.660
Amazing! Please show me it right away!

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.200
No way. What am I, stupid?

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.050
That's mean! So I'm stupid?!

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:47.250
I'm just kidding.

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:51.140
The real special move uses
a different method of rolling.

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:50.540
My legs!

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:52.920
The low altitude rolling break.

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:52.170
My legs!

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:53.750
My legs!

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:54.550
That sounds really strong!

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:55.380
My legs!

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:58.090
The perfect move for someone as naive as you.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:01.250
You tricked me twice!

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:04.710
I think it fits for someone who doesn't
understand until things are explained.

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:06.950
Teach me something real!

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:08.730
You're such a pain.

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:10.270
How about playing dead?

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:11.560
Bears!

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:21.440
That's the wrong method for dealing with a bear!

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:25.960
I heard that you're supposed to move back
slowly while maintaining eye contact.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:31.280
<i>Crap! I almost forgot what I was asking her!</i>

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:34.230
Can you at least teach me
how to get out of a headlock?

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:36.070
How to get out...?

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:36.880
Yeah.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:38.570
Just so you know,

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:42.780
once you're in a headlock, you're
not supposed to be able to get out.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:46.600
That's why you gotta keep moving
so your enemy can't use them.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:48.070
I see...

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:50.990
But biting your enemy to make
your escape is another option.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:51.930
I see!

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:53.620
Let's practice it now!

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:54.550
No way.

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:56.840
Why would I want to be bitten by you?

00:04:57.670 --> 00:05:00.860
If you don't, then I'll start biting!

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:03.210
H-Huh?

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:05.130
Where do I bite in this situation?!

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:06.620
How about your tongue?

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:08.200
Ah! I got it!

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.620
I've seen in manga that you
can escape by tickling them.

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:16.670
All right! Bring it on!

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:19.740
Damn it! Damn it!

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:21.600
Damn it! What do I do?

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:22.380
Damn it!

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:24.750
Lunchtime.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:34.480
I bought some nunchucks by mail order!

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.770
I wanted them after seeing this movie.

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:38.880
<i>She let that stuff get to her head again?</i>

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:41.150
So, here you go!

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:42.270
What?

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:43.390
Use 'em.

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:44.860
Use them yourself.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:48.870
But I wanna see you swing
them around and hit yourself.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:57.010
All right, I don't mind.

00:05:57.010 --> 00:05:58.780
But my form is perfect.

00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:03.840
See?

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.430
You should've hit yourself!

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:12.190
Sonya-chan, you have no idea how to use these!

00:06:12.190 --> 00:06:13.770
<i>This</i> is how you do it!

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:24.390
Please use them like that...

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:25.860
You're an idiot.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:34.160
On the subject of nunchucks...

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:37.030
Today, I made a nunchuck lunch!

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:39.380
How are these related?

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:43.210
Actually, it's just sushi rolls.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:44.680
I think they came out good.

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:46.820
Try one, Sonya-chan!

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:47.760
Here.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:48.930
Gotcha!

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:50.630
Those are the nunchucks!

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:52.450
Sucks to be you!

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:55.590
Huh?!

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.350
Do you want them back?

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:01.820
I'm sorry.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.480
Guess there's no helping it.

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:04.270
Here.

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:05.740
Thanks!

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:08.490
Dummy!

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:10.250
Idiot!

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:17.640
The crows took it!

00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:20.150
You're a pro and yet you let it happen twice!

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:21.260
So lame!

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:22.590
You're annoying!

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:25.560
You're not getting away!

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:28.220
Awesome!

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:54.680
Since it's after school, let's go to the crepe
shop in the big park on our way home!

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:56.630
Like high school girls would!

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:00.570
Even though you forced me along.

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:01.390
Now, now.

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:03.580
These are supposed to be really good.

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:05.250
Anyway,

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:08.010
we're not lost, are we?

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:13.220
Well, you see, this forest is a shortcut to the park...

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:22.690
We're finally out.

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:24.280
I'm exhausted.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:26.570
Hey, look! There it is!

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:28.530
Welcome.

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:30.830
What would you like, Missy?

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:39.180
I hear adding sauce to your crepe is all the rage!

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:42.110
If this is the wrong place, I'll kill you.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:47.750
The crepe shop was nearby.

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:47.110
The crepe shop was nearby.

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:51.040
I'm gonna go buy a drink.

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:55.020
What should I get...?

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:00.290
"A bear has escaped from the local zoo."

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:04.810
"There's a chance that it is still lurking in the woods."

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:12.360
I just had a really bad feeling...

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:15.070
Like some idiot somewhere just set up a flag.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:18.910
Sonya-chan will be so scared once I tell her!

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:20.490
Sonya-chan!

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:22.480
There's supposedly a—

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:24.210
—bear!!

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:26.840
How'd you know? I didn't finish.

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:44.600
You idiot! Hurry up and run!

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:47.670
You said yourself that was the
wrong way to deal with them!

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:50.320
The bear is really...!

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:51.740
Calm down!

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:55.740
It's coming towards me for some reason.

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:56.850
I got it!

00:09:56.850 --> 00:09:59.240
He's reacting to your crepe.

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:00.290
I see!

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:01.980
It's honey-flavored!

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:03.150
Just toss that—

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:06.630
All right! Now it's gone!

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:07.500
You <i>idiot</i>!

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:10.160
You were supposed to throw it to the bear and run while you had the chance!

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:11.120
The crepe's delicious!

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:12.090
Shut up!!

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:14.920
Do something, Sonya-chan!

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:17.420
You know about killing tigers and bears, don't you?!

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:18.800
Those are just martial art names!

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:20.760
I have no other choice...

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:32.280
She ran away!

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:35.470
What do I do? What do I do?!

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:39.730
It seems that you're in quite the predicament.

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:41.200
Is that you, Agiri-san?

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:46.210
If I help you, will you treat me to a crepe?

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:48.020
Yes! I will!

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:51.220
I am at your service, then.

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:51.840
Huh?

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:59.020
Would you like to purchase this Earth ninjutsu set?

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:01.800
No thanks! Just hurry, please!

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:02.830
All right, then.

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:06.020
Ninja technique: The Disappearing Bear.

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:12.310
This technique is the same as what you see on
TV to make airplanes and buildings disappear.

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:15.910
That doesn't sound like a ninja
technique at all, but please do it!

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:21.430
I will now hide the bear off in the distance.

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:25.850
One, two, three...!

00:11:26.590 --> 00:11:30.400
And now we remove the cloth.

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:32.130
See? The bear is gone.

00:11:32.130 --> 00:11:34.170
It's gotten even closer!

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:36.420
Huuuh?

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:40.820
I thought it would wander off while it was hidden.

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:42.220
Oopsie.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:44.160
It wasn't even a magic trick?!

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:49.600
I'll have to use a special technique for such a foe.

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:52.610
Fire jutsu.

00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:58.080
I'll just buy the crepe myself.

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:00.430
This seems a bit too difficult.

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:05.350
Please don't be ninja-like only
when you need to escape!

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:07.620
Sonya-chan!

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:09.700
Come down and fight it!

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.750
I hate animals!

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:14.230
Hey, stop that!

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:18.360
Help me!

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:19.010
H-Hey! Get out of here!

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:30.020
Commemoration photo.

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:32.020
Don't let it get to your head.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:36.190
The bear was then returned to the zoo.

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:42.280
One day.

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:52.730
When you get hit with a paper fan, it makes a loud noise,

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:55.420
but it doesn't really hurt.

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:57.880
So I thought....

00:12:58.050 --> 00:12:59.710
Here. This is for you.

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:00.880
What's this?

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:03.680
No way! How do you not know what a paper fan is?!

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:05.220
So lame!

00:13:08.270 --> 00:13:12.940
What's with you, giving this to me?

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:15.610
N-No, that's not what I meant!

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:19.140
<i>Sonya-chan is really bad with dogs!</i>

00:13:19.140 --> 00:13:21.450
<i>I can use that when she gets mad at me!</i>

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:30.360
Paw!

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:48.450
That's annoying.

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:52.110
If you hold your breath for a while, it'll go away.

00:13:52.110 --> 00:13:53.260
Really?

00:13:57.890 --> 00:14:01.050
I can't hold my breath for that long.

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:01.810
Ah, jeez!

00:14:02.470 --> 00:14:04.390
You give up too easily.

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:07.970
See? They went away.

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:11.310
Huh? What's wrong?

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:29.390
A bee!

00:14:44.180 --> 00:14:45.770
Sonya-chan, look!

00:14:45.770 --> 00:14:46.730
ESP!

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:49.230
Stop with the jokes and get rid of it!

00:14:49.580 --> 00:14:53.060
Are you troubled by the disposal of a bee?

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:54.610
Agiri-san!

00:14:54.610 --> 00:14:58.870
I'll use my ninjutsu and do something about it.

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:00.030
Yay!

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:05.120
Please watch.

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:08.250
Ninja technique: Disappearing Bee.

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:12.550
One, two...

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:16.740
And just like that, the bee is gone.

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:17.510
You're right!

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:20.350
And mysteriously,

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:25.460
it found its way into your clothing.

00:15:26.010 --> 00:15:28.370
It's actually still here.

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:31.020
Get rid of it!

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:37.500
Take care!

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:40.230
Don't come back again!

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:42.320
By the way...

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:45.240
would you like to purchase some ninja goods?

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:46.740
Again?

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:48.750
Five-colored rice.

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:52.710
You place them on the ground
and write out a coded message.

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:56.800
What human would have a use
for that in this day and age?

00:15:56.800 --> 00:15:59.160
I don't know a thing about codes, either.

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:01.220
Don't worry.

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:05.390
See? You can use them like that.

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:07.010
That's not a code!

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:10.090
Don't you have anything more practical?

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:12.280
Then...

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:15.980
How about this water jutsu set?

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:18.470
That's just as useless!

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:21.440
And it's the same scam as before!

00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:24.090
Are you not satisfied?

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:25.490
No, I'm not.

00:16:26.490 --> 00:16:29.120
This is my most valued one.

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:32.830
It's a secret ninja tool that will help you get rich fast.

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:35.460
It's just a lottery ticket, but I'll take it.

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:38.650
Loss.

00:16:40.130 --> 00:16:43.020
And again, after school.

00:16:48.760 --> 00:16:50.170
Watch out!

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:58.140
You should've just dodged it!

00:16:58.520 --> 00:17:00.400
I thought it would stop!

00:17:00.670 --> 00:17:03.430
If that were me, I would've easily dodged—

00:17:06.320 --> 00:17:07.740
My bad!

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:18.970
A balloon.

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:22.290
Do you want to get it back?

00:17:22.290 --> 00:17:22.710
Yeah.

00:17:22.710 --> 00:17:23.890
Go get it.

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:25.390
What do you mean, "Go get it"?

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:28.840
You offered to help, so follow it through.

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:30.500
Meanie!

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:43.420
The balloon's gonna shrink anyway, so who cares!

00:17:43.420 --> 00:17:44.380
Hey now.

00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:46.690
All right, I'll use this!

00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:58.040
Wasn't that obvious?

00:17:58.040 --> 00:18:00.000
I-I'm sorry.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.380
I'll buy you a new one.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:06.040
It's fine. That wasn't mine, anyway.

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:08.340
I was just watching it.

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:16.510
Well, whatever.

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:17.550
You sure?

00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:19.730
Let's play for a bit!

00:18:19.730 --> 00:18:20.990
Why?

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:24.770
We're already here, so we
should play your favorite game!

00:18:24.770 --> 00:18:26.010
And what is that?

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:27.040
Tag.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:28.280
I don't like that game!

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:30.940
But you're always chasing me.

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:32.730
Because you're always pissing me off!

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:34.390
Not because I like it!

00:18:34.390 --> 00:18:35.880
Oh, is that so?

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:38.190
Let's play hide-and-seek, then.

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:41.660
When I find you, consider yourself dead.

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:43.030
Don't worry!

00:18:43.030 --> 00:18:46.720
I'm good at hiding, so you'll never find me.

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:50.320
<i>I always get left behind because they can't find me.</i>

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:55.320
I'll count to ten, so go hide!

00:18:56.560 --> 00:19:01.140
One! Two! Three!

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:03.900
This sucks, so... ten!

00:19:04.730 --> 00:19:07.330
Are you going to count properly or not?

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:09.860
Oh... you're still here?

00:19:10.770 --> 00:19:13.210
I messed up my counting!

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:14.280
Liar.

00:19:14.580 --> 00:19:17.250
Or do you really not know how to count?

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:18.750
No way.

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:21.080
If you want to play, do it seriously.

00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:23.300
I'm sorry, I'll do it properly.

00:19:23.880 --> 00:19:32.050
One! Two! Three! Four! Five!

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:31.620
All right, I'll go home.

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:35.150
She's a waste of time.

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:37.150
Onee-chan!

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:40.020
You're the girl from earlier?

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:42.270
You dropped your toy.

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:44.230
Catch!

00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:45.840
Stop! Don't throw it!

00:19:45.840 --> 00:19:48.130
I thought it was a tossing game.

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:50.740
It can be tossed, but it's not a game.

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:53.390
Enough, just give it back.

00:19:53.190 --> 00:20:00.860
Nooooo!

00:19:53.390 --> 00:19:54.400
It's dangerous.

00:20:03.150 --> 00:20:05.650
Hey, don't scream like that!

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:06.380
It'll be bad if anyone saw.

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:09.020
Will you play with me, then?

00:20:10.360 --> 00:20:11.470
Ten!

00:20:11.470 --> 00:20:13.640
All right, I counted to ten this time!

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:16.470
Now, where could she be?

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:21.020
Wait! Wait! Wait! Wait!

00:20:22.020 --> 00:20:23.420
Run!

00:20:23.420 --> 00:20:24.710
What the hell was that for?!

00:20:24.710 --> 00:20:27.570
You demon! Targeting such a little girl?!

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:32.190
No, we were just playing tag, for some reason.

00:20:32.190 --> 00:20:34.400
Oh. Is that right?

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:35.200
Huh?

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:37.180
What about our game of hide-and-seek?

00:20:37.180 --> 00:20:38.450
We'll play that later.

00:20:39.190 --> 00:20:43.210
Sheesh! I was playing hide-and-seek with her first!

00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:45.590
Let's play together, then.

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:46.170
Sure.

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:48.550
All right, we're going to hide!

00:20:48.550 --> 00:20:50.510
Don't go deciding that.

00:20:50.630 --> 00:20:52.470
Rock, paper...

00:20:52.630 --> 00:20:55.470
Yay! You're it!

00:20:54.030 --> 00:20:55.970
Yay! Yay!

00:20:55.970 --> 00:20:57.970
All right, go hide!

00:20:56.300 --> 00:21:00.060
Three... Four...

00:21:13.920 --> 00:21:17.060
Sheesh. Why am I doing this...?

00:21:17.990 --> 00:21:20.020
Why aren't you hiding?

00:21:20.020 --> 00:21:23.010
It's late, so I'm going to go home.

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:23.910
Oh.

00:21:23.910 --> 00:21:25.450
Be careful on your way home.

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:28.540
Bye-bye!

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:32.670
I guess I'll go home, too.

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:35.860
Damn!

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:42.570
It feels like I've been left alone...

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:08.570
Moves, Nunchucks, Bear, Balloon.
